WEBVTT

00:36.963 --> 00:39.425
<i>We now return to Jackass.</i>

00:39.592 --> 00:41.344
<i>Hello. My name's Johnny Knoxville...</i>

00:41.511 --> 00:43.888
<i>...and I'm gonna take
a shotgun blast to the face.</i>

00:44.055 --> 00:45.181
<i>Okay, ready?</i>

00:50.938 --> 00:51.980
<i>God.</i>

00:53.690 --> 00:56.736
These guys are hilarious.
They do so much funny stuff.

00:56.903 --> 00:58.321
Hey, you know what?

00:58.488 --> 01:01.324
We should try some of that stuff
here at home.

01:01.491 --> 01:03.994
I don't know.
That skull-and-crossbones warning...

01:04.161 --> 01:07.039
...before the show was pretty clear
about not doing that.

01:07.206 --> 01:11.043
Cleveland, shut up. I saw something
on TV that I wanna imitate.

01:12.754 --> 01:13.797
Peter, what are you...?

01:13.964 --> 01:16.466
What are you boys doing up there?
Get off the roof.

01:16.633 --> 01:19.469
<i>Go back in the house, Lois.
We're being Jackass. Ready?</i>

01:19.636 --> 01:20.680
We're rolling.

01:20.846 --> 01:25.268
<i>I'm Peter Griffin,
and this is Shopping-Cart Roof...</i>

01:25.434 --> 01:29.690
<i>Roof-Shopping-Cart Guys.</i>

01:29.856 --> 01:31.608
<i>Okay, go.</i>

01:32.317 --> 01:34.319
<i>Ow. Ow. Ow.</i>

01:36.281 --> 01:38.032
- My God.
- Oh, my God. Are you okay?

01:38.199 --> 01:41.077
I don't know. I don't know.
What does it look like?

01:41.244 --> 01:43.329
What do I do? What do...? Aah.

01:43.496 --> 01:45.666
What is that? What is that?
I feel something.

01:45.833 --> 01:49.128
It's your spine, dude. It got, like,
yanked up a bunch of notches.

01:49.295 --> 01:53.049
I'm scared. I'm scared.
I'm scared. I'm scare...

01:53.216 --> 01:55.719
- Aah! Oh, God!
- Does this get fixed with ice or heat?

01:55.885 --> 01:58.096
Ice now, heat later.

01:58.263 --> 02:01.017
<i>I'm Glenn Quagmire,
and this is Bee Bush.</i>

02:01.183 --> 02:03.436
<i>All right, what'd you do
to yourself, Quagmire?</i>

02:03.602 --> 02:06.355
<i>Well, I just covered
my entire private area with honey.</i>

02:06.522 --> 02:09.151
<i>Now we're just waiting
for the bees. Heh.</i>

02:09.318 --> 02:13.030
<i>- Giggity.
- All right, here they come.</i>

02:13.238 --> 02:16.616
<i>Heh. Okay. Okay, they're on there.
Let's just...</i>

02:16.784 --> 02:20.330
<i>Just... Nobody move.
All right? Nobody do nothing.</i>

02:20.496 --> 02:22.415
<i>Just... Don't wanna make them mad.</i>

02:23.833 --> 02:25.753
<i>Ha-ha-ha.
- Stop it. Stop it. Knock it off.</i>

02:25.919 --> 02:28.464
<i>We wouldn't want the bees to get mad.
I hate you, bees.</i>

02:28.630 --> 02:30.299
<i>- I hate you, bees.
- Oh, stop it.</i>

02:30.466 --> 02:32.969
<i>- I hate you, bees.
- Knock it off. I'm serious. Stop.</i>

02:33.136 --> 02:35.013
<i>- I hate you, bees.
- Stop. That's enough.</i>

02:35.180 --> 02:37.390
<i>Just get them off.
Put them back in the hive.</i>

02:37.557 --> 02:40.101
<i>Yeah, enough is enough.
Cleveland, open the hive.</i>

02:40.268 --> 02:43.022
All right, Quagmire,
bring them over here.

02:59.582 --> 03:00.625
Oh, my.

03:03.920 --> 03:06.799
<i>Aah! What the fuck?
Why would you do that?</i>

03:08.592 --> 03:10.761
Hey, you guys,
Lois says it's time for dinner.

03:20.897 --> 03:24.235
<i>Peter, this is not safe at all.
- Shut up, Brian. Just keep filming.</i>

03:24.401 --> 03:28.155
<i>I'm Peter Griffin,
and I am the Greatest American Hero.</i>

03:28.322 --> 03:32.911
<i>My special power is being somehow
memorable after a very short run on TV.</i>

03:55.395 --> 03:57.647
- Get some, Peter!
- Nice job on that ramp, Joe.

03:57.814 --> 04:01.734
- Lf there's one thing I know, it's ramps.
- Wait, guys, I think he's really hurt.

04:01.901 --> 04:04.655
Help! Help! I think my arm is broken!

04:17.711 --> 04:20.214
Ow! My back. I can't move.

04:34.896 --> 04:38.443
I thought I was gonna die. Aah!

04:39.861 --> 04:41.571
Yeah. Yeah, that's good.

04:46.201 --> 04:48.787
You know, I'd expect
this kind of behavior from you...

04:48.954 --> 04:51.625
...but you have no business
endangering Brian like that.

04:51.791 --> 04:53.668
- Thank you.
- He jumped into that lake...

04:53.835 --> 04:56.963
...to try and save your life,
and he's 8 years old, Peter.

04:57.130 --> 05:00.843
- Eight. That's 56 in human years.
- Okay, Lois.

05:01.010 --> 05:03.054
I mean, why do you think
he almost drowned?

05:03.220 --> 05:06.557
He's old, Peter. Plus, he drinks
and he smokes all the time.

05:06.724 --> 05:10.020
So take that 56 and make it 79,
at least.

05:10.187 --> 05:13.315
Why are you making such a big deal
out of this? I was just tired.

05:13.482 --> 05:15.985
That's how it begins.
Then the next thing you know...

05:16.152 --> 05:19.072
...I'm making Peter dig a hole,
and you're in a pillowcase.

05:19.238 --> 05:22.867
You're out of your mind. Brian's young,
and I'm gonna prove it to you.

05:26.246 --> 05:27.456
Hey, youthful guy.

05:27.623 --> 05:31.168
How is your "bur-usiness" on
this aggressively redonkulous morning?

05:31.335 --> 05:33.004
What are you talking about, Peter?

05:33.171 --> 05:35.715
Don't you mean,
"'Tis-alking' about, P. Dudey?"

05:35.882 --> 05:39.219
You don't have to be formal with me.
I know how you young people talk.

05:39.386 --> 05:41.806
Peter, I'm not old,
but I'm not that young either.

05:41.972 --> 05:44.392
We should sip Bacardi
like it's your birthday.

05:44.558 --> 05:45.643
What does that mean?

05:45.810 --> 05:50.232
It means that this damn thing
doesn't work at all.

05:53.026 --> 05:56.154
- Peter, what are you doing?
- Lf movies have taught me anything...

05:56.322 --> 06:00.535
...it's that young people are constantly
being antagonized by preppy '80s bullies.

06:00.701 --> 06:03.079
- What?
- What are you gonna do about it?

06:03.246 --> 06:06.458
- Peter, this doesn't make sense.
- You know what doesn't make sense?

06:06.625 --> 06:10.629
Some new-kid jerk moving into my town
and being worse than me at karate.

06:10.796 --> 06:13.383
- Peter, you don't know karate.
- Stay away from Muffy.

06:13.550 --> 06:15.927
She's my girlfriend.
She just doesn't know it yet.

06:16.094 --> 06:18.638
Excuse me,
I gotta go get yelled at by my father...

06:18.805 --> 06:21.934
...because we're more alike
than we know.

06:37.326 --> 06:41.164
- Peter, did you have fun with Brian?
- No, Lois, he was a wet blanket.

06:41.330 --> 06:44.709
And I'm starting to think
you might be right. Brian's getting old.

06:44.876 --> 06:48.130
He's not the dog he used to be,
and I'll have to get used to it.

06:48.297 --> 06:50.674
Just like I got used to my acrylic nails.

06:55.930 --> 06:58.892
Stanion, Winestock and Riesman.

06:59.058 --> 07:00.685
Hey, LaRonda.

07:00.852 --> 07:04.440
No, I got four people on hold,
but I can talk.

07:08.485 --> 07:11.740
Good morning, everybody.
Brian, I have something to say.

07:11.907 --> 07:14.701
I'm sorry I've been so preoccupied
with your age.

07:14.868 --> 07:17.747
Well, look, Peter, don't worry.
Let's just forget about it.

07:17.914 --> 07:20.917
Fantastic. And to help us
forget about it, family...

07:21.083 --> 07:23.920
...I'd like to introduce New Brian.

07:24.086 --> 07:25.129
Hey, gang.

07:25.296 --> 07:28.091
Whose leg do you have to hump
to get a hug around here?

07:31.678 --> 07:33.932
Oh, I like him.

07:40.313 --> 07:42.399
- You got a new dog?
- Yes, sir.

07:42.566 --> 07:45.444
- But I'm the dog.
- Well, now that you're getting older...

07:45.611 --> 07:47.946
...New Brian's here
to take some of the load off.

07:48.113 --> 07:49.782
- Can he do tricks?
- Oh, you bet.

07:49.948 --> 07:53.870
He's trained to fetch, roll over, and make
you feel really good about yourself.

07:54.037 --> 07:58.124
Wow, Meg and Chris. I can't decide
which one of your hats I like better.

07:59.710 --> 08:03.172
I can't believe you got a new dog.
What about me?

08:03.339 --> 08:04.674
Hey, you're still my buddy.

08:04.840 --> 08:07.177
New Brian is just a new friend
for the family.

08:07.344 --> 08:11.098
You guys are gonna get along better
than Abraham Lincoln and his neighbor.

08:13.767 --> 08:17.522
Hey, Dale, I noticed your lawn's
getting a little high.

08:17.689 --> 08:20.692
Yeah. I used to have a guy
for that, dick.

08:20.858 --> 08:22.485
Okay, now, you have a good one.

08:34.290 --> 08:37.085
My word,
what a gorgeous way to wake up.

08:37.252 --> 08:38.294
I hope you don't mind.

08:38.461 --> 08:41.382
I checked the time
your alarm was set for, and I shut it off.

08:41.549 --> 08:44.385
I figured this might be
a more gentle way to start the day.

08:44.552 --> 08:47.264
Oh, that is so thoughtful, New Brian.

08:51.893 --> 08:54.521
I'll start up again in nine minutes.

08:55.815 --> 08:58.943
Hey, Meg. I know how you like
to let off steam once in a while.

08:59.110 --> 09:01.696
- So I got you a journal.
- You got me a journal?

09:01.863 --> 09:06.034
Actually, I got you two of them:
My right ear and my left ear.

09:06.201 --> 09:07.369
Fire away.

09:07.536 --> 09:11.833
<i>Dear diary: Today, at the school library,
I saw a picture in National Geographic...</i>

09:12.000 --> 09:15.044
...of a woman with nipples
that cover most of her breasts too.

09:15.211 --> 09:19.174
- And suddenly, I didn't feel so alone.
- You know what it sounds like to me?

09:19.340 --> 09:22.178
Sounds like the woman in that picture
was pretty beautiful.

09:23.387 --> 09:25.055
All right, I'll see you at dinner.

09:25.222 --> 09:27.349
- Think fast.
- Wow, deodorant.

09:27.516 --> 09:29.895
- Are you sure I'm old enough?
- Oh, I think so.

09:30.061 --> 09:34.065
I'm gonna make you
a little less gross every day.

09:36.485 --> 09:39.864
- Hey, New Brian. Oh, you have a guitar.
- Yep.

09:40.031 --> 09:43.534
In fact, I wrote a new song today,
and I wanna hear what you think of it.

09:43.701 --> 09:45.495
Where did you find the time for that?

09:45.662 --> 09:48.790
Peter, inspiration
doesn't have a schedule.

09:48.957 --> 09:51.460
<i>I don't like fancy learning books</i>

09:51.627 --> 09:53.880
<i>I don't like apple tarts</i>

09:54.047 --> 09:56.466
<i>I don't like cozy breakfast nooks</i>

09:56.633 --> 10:00.554
<i>I don't like modern arts</i>

10:00.721 --> 10:01.805
<i>Well, I like farts</i>

10:01.972 --> 10:03.057
Ah!

10:03.224 --> 10:04.391
<i>Yes, I like farts</i>

10:04.558 --> 10:06.018
<i>I like long farts, short farts</i>

10:06.185 --> 10:08.103
<i>Wet farts, your farts
I like farts</i>

10:08.270 --> 10:10.148
<i>- If you've got heart
- Oh, I've got heart</i>

10:10.315 --> 10:12.275
<i>- Let's hear those farts
- How do I start?</i>

10:12.442 --> 10:16.237
<i>Well, Peter
I will help you get your farting started</i>

10:27.417 --> 10:30.545
Brian, I went out for a run this morning,
and I found this stick.

10:30.712 --> 10:33.049
- I thought you might like it.
- Wow, thanks a lot.

10:33.216 --> 10:34.926
And I got you this bag of weed.

10:35.093 --> 10:37.804
I don't smoke it myself,
but I sure won't judge you.

10:37.971 --> 10:41.183
- Gosh, thanks.
- Check you later, handsome guy.

10:41.350 --> 10:44.019
Well, I wasn't sure
about this new-dog thing at first...

10:44.186 --> 10:46.689
...but I gotta tell you,
he's a really terrific guy.

10:46.855 --> 10:49.109
You poor damn fool.

10:49.275 --> 10:51.987
- What?
- You have no idea what's going on here.

10:52.153 --> 10:54.948
He's not just a delightful new friend
for the family.

10:55.115 --> 10:57.952
- He's your replacement.
- Oh, come on, that's ridiculous.

10:58.119 --> 11:01.455
You're getting old, and they know it.
You're no longer the cover girl.

11:01.622 --> 11:04.792
Look at Carol Alt. That's what...
You're Carol Alt.

11:04.959 --> 11:06.753
- I'm through listening to you.
- Fine.

11:06.920 --> 11:10.090
Think what you want,
aging supermodel Carol Alt.

11:10.257 --> 11:11.425
Carol, come in here.

11:11.591 --> 11:14.053
<i>They're saying your name
on the Family Man.</i>

11:14.220 --> 11:15.263
What?
Huh?

11:15.430 --> 11:16.472
- What?
- Huh?

11:16.639 --> 11:18.433
- What?
I forget.

11:18.599 --> 11:21.603
And besides, Brian, the evidence
is all right in front of your nose.

11:21.770 --> 11:24.523
Ha-ha-ha. That's hilarious, New Brian.

11:24.690 --> 11:27.067
Now do your impression
of Punky Brewster's father.

11:27.234 --> 11:28.652
Punky.

11:28.819 --> 11:31.114
- Oh, Punky.
- Ha-ha-ha!

11:31.281 --> 11:34.284
Oh, Punky,
you have a dog named Brandon.

11:36.453 --> 11:38.539
"Hi. I'm Carol Alt for PoliGrip. "

11:38.706 --> 11:39.749
They did it again.

11:39.915 --> 11:41.292
<i>Who?
- The Family Man.</i>

11:41.459 --> 11:45.421
<i>Is that the one with the fish?
- No, that's American Boy!.</i>

11:49.342 --> 11:50.427
Okay. Relax, Brian.

11:50.594 --> 11:54.098
There's no way they'd replace you.
But it couldn't hurt to remind them...

11:54.265 --> 11:57.185
...how much they value you
as a family member.

11:57.351 --> 11:59.437
- Hey, buddy.
- Uh...

11:59.604 --> 12:01.939
- Hey.
- I just wanted to check in with you.

12:02.106 --> 12:04.234
You know,
sometimes life happens so fast...

12:04.401 --> 12:06.695
...we miss the most important part,
which is sharing it.

12:06.862 --> 12:09.656
- Uh-huh.
- You see, Chris, I care about you.

12:09.823 --> 12:12.619
And if there's ever anything
you ever wanna talk about...

12:12.785 --> 12:16.039
...or if you just want some company,
I'm here for you.

12:16.206 --> 12:19.418
- So how's it hanging?
- Uh...

12:19.585 --> 12:21.504
- Okay.
- Hey, what do you got here?

12:21.670 --> 12:26.133
<i>Oh, Maxim.
That Jessica Biel sure is a cutie.</i>

12:27.135 --> 12:28.887
You were masturbating
when I came in.

12:29.054 --> 12:30.180
Yeah.

12:30.347 --> 12:33.808
- So how's it hang...?
- Get out!

12:33.975 --> 12:35.311
Gotcha.

12:38.689 --> 12:41.567
Okay, everybody,
tonight, I've got a real treat for you.

12:41.734 --> 12:43.904
We've all seen
your compilation video, Brian:

12:44.071 --> 12:47.574
Shatner singing "Rocket Man," drunk
Orson Welles doing that commercial...

12:47.741 --> 12:51.371
...Sylvester Stallone in that porno,
and Bill Cosby beating up that midget.

12:51.537 --> 12:54.165
- I don't remember that last one.
- It's freaking brutal.

12:54.332 --> 12:55.750
For no reason, you know?

12:55.917 --> 12:58.169
Poor guy's sitting there
eating his Snack Pack.

12:58.336 --> 13:01.215
Bill Cosby runs in out of nowhere
and starts wailing on him.

13:01.382 --> 13:02.549
Didn't that guy die?

13:02.716 --> 13:04.885
These are home movies
from when I was a puppy.

13:05.052 --> 13:07.681
- He died.
- Okay, look, just watch.

13:22.989 --> 13:25.075
Aww...

13:26.326 --> 13:28.120
Oh, look at him sleep.

13:28.287 --> 13:31.123
Oh, I wonder
what he's dreaming about.

13:31.289 --> 13:32.667
Shut up, Meg.

13:34.085 --> 13:35.128
Oh, did you hear that?

13:35.294 --> 13:37.922
- He farted.
- Just like in the song.

13:40.843 --> 13:45.514
Aah! What the hell is the matter
with you? Outside. Outside now.

13:47.516 --> 13:49.853
Well, I hate to say I told you so, but...

13:50.020 --> 13:52.522
Wait a minute,
I love saying I told you so. Ha. Doy.

13:52.689 --> 13:54.733
Ha. " Hey, Stewie Griffin,
meet Stewie Griffin. "

13:54.899 --> 13:56.777
Ha. "Nice to meet you. "
"Charmed, I'm sure. "

13:56.944 --> 13:58.904
"Great outfit. " "Oh, go on. "
"No, it is. "

13:59.071 --> 14:02.241
So what if there's a new dog?
Lots of families have two dogs.

14:02.408 --> 14:04.995
I thought maybe
we could spend the afternoon together.

14:05.162 --> 14:06.997
- Really? That'd be great.
- Awesome.

14:07.164 --> 14:09.124
- Because, uh, I got this new gun.
- Here we go.

14:09.291 --> 14:13.171
I thought we could go deep in the woods
where no one would ever think to look.

14:13.337 --> 14:14.380
Oh, boy.

14:14.547 --> 14:16.007
- And, uh, just shoot it.
- Awkward.

14:16.174 --> 14:18.801
You know, like so far in
that no one can hear gunfire.

14:18.968 --> 14:20.470
- A little on the nose.
- Or screaming.

14:20.637 --> 14:23.223
Uh... I don't think so, Peter.

14:23.390 --> 14:25.267
It's like he thinks
I'm gonna shoot him.

14:25.434 --> 14:28.688
He's acting all crazy,
like Quagmire when he drunk-dials me.

14:31.524 --> 14:35.195
<i>- Hello?
Hey. What are you doing?</i>

14:35.361 --> 14:38.407
<i>- Quagmire, I'm sleeping.
- Yeah, I was just out with Joe.</i>

14:38.574 --> 14:41.368
<i>- What are you doing?
- I just told you.</i>

14:41.535 --> 14:44.121
<i>Oh, that's right. I just asked that.</i>

14:44.288 --> 14:47.125
<i>I forgot. Hey.
Hey, this song made me think of you.</i>

14:47.292 --> 14:49.878
<i>So li... Wait. Listen to this song.</i>

14:53.257 --> 14:54.300
<i>Isn't that awesome?</i>

14:54.467 --> 14:56.135
<i>You said you weren't
gonna call him.</i>

14:56.302 --> 14:57.804
<i>It's not him, you big bully.</i>

14:57.970 --> 15:02.935
<i>Joe told me not to call you.
So, what are you doing?</i>

15:09.359 --> 15:11.778
Everyone,
I have an announcement to make.

15:11.945 --> 15:16.115
- I've decided I'm leaving.
- What? Leaving? Brian, why?

15:16.282 --> 15:19.328
Well, you know, I feel like
I've sort of run my course here.

15:19.495 --> 15:22.498
And, you know, besides,
there's a whole big world out there...

15:22.665 --> 15:24.041
...and it's time I saw it.

15:24.208 --> 15:27.045
But, Brian, you live here.
This is your home.

15:27.212 --> 15:29.506
I know, but I've thought about this
long and hard, and...

15:29.673 --> 15:31.466
Ha-ha-ha. "Long and hard. "

15:31.633 --> 15:33.677
I'm sorry, Brian.
Please, please, continue.

15:33.844 --> 15:37.390
- This is just something I have to do.
- Well, where will you go?

15:37.557 --> 15:40.810
Well, I haven't decided that yet,
but I promise I'll be in touch.

15:40.977 --> 15:43.188
- Ha-ha-ha.
- Wait, how is that one dirty?

15:43.355 --> 15:45.816
It's... I was remembering
"long and hard. "

15:45.983 --> 15:50.863
Well, if your mind is made up about this,
Brian, then I wish you the best of luck.

15:51.030 --> 15:54.200
I hope this move
won't be a boner for you.

15:54.367 --> 15:56.786
- Peter?
- Hmm?

15:57.036 --> 15:58.831
- What?
- I was just saying to Brian:

15:58.998 --> 16:01.750
- "I hope this move won't be a boner. "
- I would agree.

16:01.917 --> 16:04.461
- I hope he finds what he's looking for.
- Okay.

16:04.628 --> 16:08.300
Well, we're gonna miss you, Brian.

16:13.805 --> 16:16.100
Hey, everybody,
let's watch this tape. Okay.

16:16.267 --> 16:19.770
There's the midget just sitting there.
Watch the left side of the screen.

16:19.937 --> 16:23.108
<i>I'm in a bad mood,
and I'm gonna take it out on you.</i>

16:24.526 --> 16:26.361
Oh, my God.
Well, he's obviously drunk.

16:26.528 --> 16:27.863
<i>Ow! Ow! You're hurting me.</i>

16:28.030 --> 16:31.451
<i>About which I do not care very much.</i>

16:37.707 --> 16:40.878
- Pancake?
- Oh, just a small one, thanks. Mm.

16:41.045 --> 16:44.089
My God, these are the best pancakes
I've ever had.

16:44.256 --> 16:45.841
And I've been to IHOP.

16:46.008 --> 16:48.511
These are the best pancakes
I've ever had.

16:48.678 --> 16:50.221
And I've been to Applebee's.

16:50.388 --> 16:53.099
These are the best pancakes
I've ever had.

16:53.266 --> 16:54.726
And I've been to Denny's.

16:54.893 --> 16:56.645
These pancakes are okay.

16:56.812 --> 17:00.524
Oh, boy.
I bet Brian would love these pancakes.

17:00.691 --> 17:03.320
- I wonder where he is.
- He's next door with Cleveland.

17:03.487 --> 17:05.572
I saw him on my morning paper route.

17:05.739 --> 17:07.991
I appreciate you
letting me stay with you...

17:08.158 --> 17:11.244
...but I'm perfectly capable
of going to the bathroom by myself.

17:11.412 --> 17:13.998
Sorry, but there's a leash law
in this neighborhood...

17:14.165 --> 17:16.751
...and you never know
who's watching.

17:20.172 --> 17:23.759
I'm watching you make stool.

17:27.889 --> 17:30.475
Hey, New Brian.
Oh, I see you're having pie.

17:30.642 --> 17:33.895
You know, pie isn't really pie
without Cool Whip.

17:34.521 --> 17:37.274
Everything's better with Cool Whip.

17:37.775 --> 17:39.777
- Did you hear what I said?
- What about it?

17:39.944 --> 17:42.738
It doesn't bother you
the way I pronounce it? "Cool Whip"?

17:42.905 --> 17:44.908
- No. Why would it?
- Cool Whip.

17:45.075 --> 17:47.786
- I'm putting emphasis on the H.
- Sounds right to me.

17:47.953 --> 17:50.747
- Nothing ever bothers you, does it?
- No, not really.

17:50.914 --> 17:52.083
I like everything.

17:52.250 --> 17:54.836
God, he's a bigger buzz kill
than Buzz Killington.

17:55.002 --> 17:59.257
Stewie, do you know
why W.S. Gilbert...

17:59.423 --> 18:03.428
...was frequently drunk
on his transatlantic crossings?

18:03.595 --> 18:04.638
No.

18:04.805 --> 18:08.893
Because he was quartered
on the portside.

18:11.521 --> 18:13.189
Now that I've got you...

18:13.356 --> 18:18.028
...let's both revisit the birth
of the D'Oyly Carte Opera Company.

18:28.999 --> 18:31.376
Two, three.

18:34.964 --> 18:39.635
- Okay, New Brian, you're next.
- Ha-ha-ha. Oh, no. Oh, boy. All right.

18:39.802 --> 18:43.682
Well, I can't do this alone.
Lois, I'm gonna need your help here.

18:43.849 --> 18:45.475
Oh, my God. Uh-oh.

18:45.642 --> 18:49.522
Okay. Rita Coolidge's
less-talented sister here.

18:51.524 --> 18:53.318
In what way is that a joke?

18:53.735 --> 18:55.486
- Okay. You start.
- Okay.

18:55.653 --> 18:57.948
All right. I don't know...
Am I blue or am I red?

18:58.115 --> 19:01.201
- You're blue. You're blue.
- This is crazy. Okay, I'll do it, then.

19:28.732 --> 19:30.276
Thanks for letting me stay here.

19:30.443 --> 19:33.529
- I hope I'm not in the way.
- No, no. Should be fine. Um...

19:33.696 --> 19:36.032
But, uh, listen, Brian...

19:36.199 --> 19:39.203
...I'm gonna be bringing
a Puerto Rican girl over here later...

19:39.370 --> 19:41.705
...and she's super hot and real nice.

19:41.872 --> 19:44.375
But when she was 5 years old...

19:44.541 --> 19:47.337
...her dad ran over one of her legs
with his van...

19:47.504 --> 19:52.175
...and it's still kind of messed up
in a pretty obvious, instantly visible way.

19:52.342 --> 19:54.637
Um... Please don't say anything.

19:54.804 --> 19:57.640
And try to make eye contact with her
when she wobbles in...

19:57.807 --> 19:59.433
...because I want this to work.
- Uh...

19:59.600 --> 20:01.018
Yeah, sure. No problem.

20:01.185 --> 20:03.355
I'm serious, Brian,
that leg is a train wreck.

20:03.522 --> 20:05.399
I mean, she herself is so pretty...

20:05.565 --> 20:10.195
...but that thing just looks like a string
of sausages with one empty casing in it.

20:10.363 --> 20:12.323
- I get it.
- It's quite a sight, you know?

20:12.490 --> 20:15.910
When she's not looking, you should
take a look at it, but be discreet.

20:16.077 --> 20:17.745
Yeah, I'll, uh...

20:17.912 --> 20:19.957
I'll check that out.

20:22.668 --> 20:25.671
- Stewie, what are you doing here?
- Brian, you gotta come back.

20:25.838 --> 20:29.467
- Why?
- Because New Brian is such a tool.

20:29.634 --> 20:32.554
I mean, he's so damn sweet
and saccharine and perfect...

20:32.720 --> 20:35.349
...and he's turning the family
into a bunch of douches.

20:35.516 --> 20:38.227
Well, big deal.
You always told me I was a douche.

20:38.394 --> 20:42.606
Yeah. But you were my douche, Brian.
My douche.

20:42.774 --> 20:45.193
Come back and be my douche again.

20:45.360 --> 20:49.614
- Hi. I'm looking for Glenn.
- Oh, what happened to your leg?!

20:51.909 --> 20:53.286
Damn it, Brian.

20:53.452 --> 20:54.829
Come back home, Brian.

20:54.996 --> 20:58.875
When this is all over, I'll make you some
pie with a nice dollop of Cool Whip.

20:59.042 --> 21:01.712
There it is again. Why are you putting
so much emphasis on the H?

21:03.130 --> 21:04.965
That's exactly why I miss you, Brian.

21:05.132 --> 21:08.595
Forget it. I'm not going back
as long as that new dog is there.

21:08.761 --> 21:12.181
As long as he's a part of that family,
there's no place for me.

21:12.348 --> 21:15.561
Well, I can't say I blame you.
I hate him as much as you do, Brian.

21:15.728 --> 21:19.607
He's a bad fit.
Like a crocodile at an alligator rally.

21:19.773 --> 21:22.276
Yeah, lurking in the water
with our eyes poking out.

21:22.443 --> 21:23.486
Yeah.

21:23.653 --> 21:26.656
Sneaking up on a crane or an egret
and snapping our jaws on it.

21:26.823 --> 21:27.866
Yeah.

21:28.033 --> 21:31.537
And sometimes walking out
onto a dry plain or dusty field...

21:31.704 --> 21:34.498
...because it's nice to get out
of the swamp now and then.

21:34.665 --> 21:36.042
- Yeah...
- Wait.

21:36.208 --> 21:37.793
- What?
- What? Huh?

21:37.960 --> 21:42.257
Dry plain? Dusty field?
Nice to get out of the swamp?

21:42.424 --> 21:43.800
What a croc.

21:44.217 --> 21:46.303
And that's where we get the term.

21:52.226 --> 21:55.355
Hey, New Brian. Bad news.
You gotta leave.

21:55.521 --> 21:58.067
Huh? What are you talking about?
This is my home.

21:58.233 --> 21:59.526
Nobody likes you here.

21:59.693 --> 22:02.029
Well, I disagree.
I think everybody likes me.

22:02.196 --> 22:05.659
No, we don't. We don't like your
cooking, your stupid karaoke nights...

22:05.825 --> 22:09.245
...and we especially don't like the way
you hump that chair in the den.

22:09.412 --> 22:11.456
Well, Rupert seems
to like my humping.

22:12.333 --> 22:13.834
- What did you say?
- Rupert.

22:14.001 --> 22:18.172
Humped him for two hours yesterday.
He just laid there and took it.

22:18.631 --> 22:19.965
- Did he?
- Yeah.

22:20.132 --> 22:23.929
And now every time you're sleeping
with him, he's gonna be thinking of me.

22:36.567 --> 22:39.238
"And that is why I killed myself,
chopped myself up...

22:39.405 --> 22:41.281
...and put myself in the garbage. "

22:41.448 --> 22:45.453
- Wow, he must've had some demons.
- Oh, my God. Suicide?

22:45.620 --> 22:47.831
How could we have misjudged him
so severely?

22:47.997 --> 22:50.291
Oftentimes it's the ones
who seem the happiest.

22:50.458 --> 22:53.421
Well, the upside is,
at least we have our old Brian back.

22:53.587 --> 22:56.966
From now on, buddy,
you're the only animal I care about.

22:57.133 --> 23:00.344
Hey, everybody.
I'm Bernie the Hamster.

23:00.511 --> 23:04.891
- Would you like to be my friend?
- Oh, my G...

23:05.058 --> 23:06.309
It's okay, Peter.

23:06.476 --> 23:09.313
Yay! Oh, my God. Oh, my God.
It's a hamster.

23:12.817 --> 23:15.820
We'll talk about it
when you want to talk about it.

23:15.987 --> 23:18.198
I don't blame you.

23:18.574 --> 23:22.161
I... I don't blame you.

23:22.162 --> 24:23.162
Thank you for watching «Family Guy» on
www.FOX-fan.ru